The main body is a continuous, flowing and twisted transparent ribbon. This ribbon is called the "time" ribbon. It is not a straight line. One end is composed of fragmented, scattered pieces (representing the past, the scattered time); in the middle, it constantly bends, swirls, and loops (representing the present, the repetitive daily life); at the top, it gradually gathers and extends upwards towards the faint light on the canvas (representing the future, the forward extension). The ribbon is dotted with circular light spots of varying sizes, resembling clock hands or starlight.
